      "answer": "$\\theta=30^\\circ,\\ 150^\\circ$.",
      "official_mark_scheme_text": "Use the correct $\\tan(A\\pm B)$ formula and obtain an equation in $\\tan\\theta$ — M1. Guidance: $\\frac1{\\tan\\theta}+\\frac{1-\\tan\\theta\\tan45^\\circ}{\\tan\\theta+\\tan45^\\circ}=2$; allow M1 with $\\tan45^\\circ$, giving $\\frac1{\\tan\\theta}+\\frac{1-\\tan\\theta}{\\tan\\theta+1}=2$. Obtain a correct equation in any form with values substituted — A1. Reduce to $3\\tan^2\\theta=1$, or equivalent — A1. Obtain one correct solution $30^\\circ$ — A1. Obtain the second solution $150^\\circ$ and no others in range — A1. OR use correct $\\sin(A\\pm B)$ and $\\cos(A\\pm B)$ formulae to form an equation in $\\sin\\theta$ and $\\cos\\theta$ — M1A1; reduce to $\\tan^2\\theta=\\frac13$, $\\sin^2\\theta=\\frac14$, $\\cos^2\\theta=\\frac34$ or $\\cot^2\\theta=3$, etc. — A1; obtain the two answers — A1 + A1. Total: 5.",
